        "code": {
          "text": "Right subacromial pain syndrome/impingement, likely rotator cuff overload from repetitive overhead work"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder pain and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pain for approximately 5–6 days, initially a mild ache on waking and now worsened, with a marked flare over the last 24–48 hours. Described as sharp and grabbing with movement; 7–8/10 with movement and 3/10 at rest. Anterolateral right shoulder pain radiating to the mid-humerus, not past the elbow. Worse at night; unable to lie on the right side and struggling to sleep. Aggravated by overhead reaching, putting on a jumper, reaching behind the back, reaching across the body, and hanging washing. Arm by side helps; heat pack helps a little. Partner reports patient was pacing around all night with the pain."
      }
    },
