        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported negative symptoms and history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No trauma, fall, or heavy lifting. No neck pain, paraesthesiae, chest pain, shortness of breath, fevers, sweats, weight loss, redness, or swelling. No chronic illness, previous shoulder or neck problems, diabetes, malignancy, or inflammatory arthritis reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder inspection and palpation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No deformity, swelling, or erythema. Mild tenderness at the anterolateral acromion/greater tuberosity."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder range of motion"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Active flexion approximately 120 degrees, limited by pain. Abduction approximately 90–100 degrees, with painful arc from approximately 60–120 degrees. Internal rotation behind the back limited; unable to reach bra strap. Passive range of motion near full, painful, with no hard stop."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder strength and provocative tests"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Supraspinatus testing reproduces pain, with possible slight weakness versus pain inhibition. Infraspinatus and subscapularis strength grossly intact. Hawkins positive, Neer positive, and painful arc positive."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
